## Embedded dependency fonts

[noto-sans-mono-bitmap](https://github.com/phip1611/noto-sans-mono-bitmap)
is declared by the root, `kernel/`, `libs/libgfx-ref/`, `userspace/programs/`
and `tools/console-host-tests/` manifests with requirement `0.3`, by
`libs/libgfx/` with `0.3.2`, and by `scripts/metal/efi-stub/` with the exact
pin `=0.3.2`. The kernel graphics font and console are among its consumers.
The crate code is MIT, copyright (c) 2022 Philipp Schuster; [license text](licenses/noto-sans-mono-bitmap-MIT.txt) retained from
release 0.3.2. Its README identifies the rasterized Noto Sans Mono font as
OFL-1.1. [The Noto Sans Mono OFL notice](licenses/OFL-notosansmono.txt) is included
for the font family; the exact source-font version and copyright notice for
the dependency's raster data remain unresolved. This dependency is fetched at
build time, not stored as a vendor directory in this tree.

## Unresolved provenance and license checks

- `fonts/CascadiaCode-Regular.ttf`: conflicting embedded and upstream license
  records, described above; copyright © 2021 Microsoft Corporation.
- `libs/libbreenix/src/x509/ca-certificates.der`: embedded Mozilla root CA
  certificates, sourced according to `ca_bundle.rs` from
  https://curl.se/ca/cacert.pem. The exact input snapshot and its copyright and
  license notices are absent; applicable notices for this bundled conversion
  remain unresolved, rather than inferred from today's download.
- `scripts/qemu-gl/host-renderer-attestation.patch`: its own notice assigns
  GPL-2.0-or-later to this QEMU modification. The license is identified; the
  remaining check is to retain the exact pinned upstream file copyright and
  license notices for its QEMU context before redistribution. The root license
  does not replace these terms.
- `libs/libc/ci/android-emulator-package.xml`: contains Google's Android SDK
  License Agreement in package metadata. The agreement is preserved in that
  file; the grant to redistribute this metadata itself is not established here.
- Historical compressed evidence archives under `docs/planning/` and toolchain
  patch excerpts have not been individually license-cleared. They must not be
  treated as license clearance for archived third-party content under the root
  license.
- The exact Noto source-font notices for `noto-sans-mono-bitmap` remain to be
  matched to its rasterized font version, as described above.

